{"id": "EUVD-2026-103803", "enisaUuid": "ab91731f-a3f9-34e3-a540-87773c9d0814", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: x86: Re-pend GET_NESTED_STATE_PAGES if getting said pages fails\n\nRe-pend GET_NESTED_STATE_PAGES before exiting to userspace if getting the\nnested pages fails in the KVM_RUN path.  If userspace re-runs the vCPU, and\nvmcs02 holds valid PFNs from the *previous* run of L2, then KVM could\nre-enter L2 with stale, unpinned PFNs mapped into e.g. the vAPIC page.\n\nNote, both SVM and VMX (as of commit 11722439fb20 (\"KVM: nVMX: Ensure\nKVM_REQ_GET_NESTED_STATE_PAGES is cleared on VM-Exit\") ensure the request\nis cleared on VM-Exit (including the \"forced\" case), i.e. there is no risk\nof double-mapping due to emulated VMLAUNCH/VMRESUME/VMRUN *and* the request\ntrying to map the nested pages.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:51:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:26:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/525694a6021ec6c8f7ce1f38acdf2dd77698fec1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/942192dbcd3a06695ef6b31cf10a41a21cf014d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/10180a277549339020b08000206092c07e0bff5a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98863", "GHSA-8v5w-2f74-jcch"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "12fc75c5-d638-30fc-b2c7-db396c713633", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "671ddc700fd08b94967b1e2a937020e30c838609 <525694a6021ec6c8f7ce1f38acdf2dd77698fec1"}, {"id": "3d442e08-30e7-3e0a-9283-4dfce07138e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "4039bd44-1ded-3fe2-85af-b81684b6fdf2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "62a6e20d-f0ed-3cac-9bdb-c34b4f811102", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "671ddc700fd08b94967b1e2a937020e30c838609 <942192dbcd3a06695ef6b31cf10a41a21cf014d8"}, {"id": "802acb9d-cd75-3fbf-8491-32d8ea7554c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4"}, {"id": "a875835c-c525-3cd1-b1cb-75fe685d515f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "671ddc700fd08b94967b1e2a937020e30c838609 <10180a277549339020b08000206092c07e0bff5a"}, {"id": "cd09073f-1312-3a74-a3dd-1200909f5136", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e00e4664-a4c6-38f4-9d23-0a4c7a201b05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bf78f16c-521d-3396-a669-f52b5c2db1e6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}